        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "chore(qa): verify packaged Codex cold install",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a QA coverage problem where the Codex cold-install scenario was backed by synthetic fixture behavior instead of the packaged OpenClaw product path. The taxonomy also claimed an install/first-turn race and doctor coverage that no production scenario executed.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nRoutes the cold-install scenario through the existing `codex-on-demand` Docker lane and strengthens that lane to require one successful onboarding terminal document plus the canonical SQLite install record. Removes the self-authored race scenario and its fixture-only test surface, and drops the unsupported doctor claim.\n\nAI-assisted: Yes. The implementation and production ordering decision were reviewed with Codex; no transcript is included without explicit consent.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo runtime behavior changes. Maintainers gain package-backed regression evidence that a clean OpenClaw install downloads and loads the managed Codex runtime while recording the install canonically.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs ...`: 342 focused tests passed across the touched QA, tooling, command, plugin, and production setup-ordering surfaces.\n- Post-correction catalog proof: 41 tests passed; post-rebase catalog/assertion/adapter proof: 75 tests passed.\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD`: passed.\n- Fresh autoreview after the final taxonomy correction: no accepted/actionable findings (confidence 0.87).\n- Trusted Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxp1y43hq69q6vmhxv059eh3`, exact head `e416553f9ab1d8d0b50d8d8f323c7706aa8c65a4`: `pnpm build` passed.\n- [Exact-head Testbox run](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29522830673): `pnpm test:docker:codex-on-demand` passed, including package inventory, tarball integrity/import-graph verification, clean Docker onboarding, one terminal JSON document, canonical SQLite install record, managed `@openai/codex` binary, and harness loading.\n- `pnpm check:changed` reached the Plugin SDK API baseline and failed on a pre-existing hash drift; an isolated `git archive origin/main` run on the same Testbox failed identically, so no unrelated generated hash is included here.\n",
        "branch": "fix/qa-codex-plugin-install-product-proof",
